WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.900
[Michigan Tuberculosis Association: Theodore Werle, Executive Secretary, presents]

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:15.800
[Peter Borik: The Story of the Tragedy he
Brought his Family]

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:23.800
[Scenario: Wm Kulsea, Narrator: Bob Clayton, Donald O. Buell: Director of Dramatics, Michigan State College.]

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:24.000
 

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:31.900
[Cast: Agnes... June Merz, Clara... Frances
Joyner, Mrs. Borik... Mary Philips, John...Joe Davidson]

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:32.100
 

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:37.800
[Dedicated to the fight against tuberculosis]

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:46.300
[Narrator:] The story of Agnes and Clara Borik
and their family could happen in your town,

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:50.319
right next door to you...it could happen to
the rich man and to

00:00:50.319 --> 00:00:51.550
the poor man.

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:57.339
The office worker or the farmer, a white man
or a negro. It could happen to the young,

00:00:57.339 --> 00:01:01.179
and it could happen to the aged. It could
happen to anyone.

00:01:01.179 --> 00:01:07.620
It is the story of a willful man who refused
to believe the truth. Because he stubbornly

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:11.070
and perversely rejected the truth, he brought
tragedy to those

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:13.330
closest to him.

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:18.190
He turned a deaf ear to experienced men of
medicine who sought to help him in his fight

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:19.990
against tuberculosis.

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:25.400
Instead, he chose to rely on the advice of
charlatans and quacks. It is the story of

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:29.370
Peter Borik and the heartaches he brought
his daughters, Agnes and

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:34.130
Clara.

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:39.390
The story opens on a tender note, for Clara
and Johnny Carson, a young farmer who manages

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:43.600
the Borik farm in his spare time, are in love.
They hope to be

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:48.280
married soon. Johnny is her childhood sweetheart.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:53.390
His regular job, before he took over operation
of the Borik farm, was driving a milk truck

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:58.110
for a large dairy company nearby. He still
does this when he is

00:01:58.110 --> 00:01:58.840
able.

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:04.770
Now however, Peter Borik is bedridden most
of the time, and unable to work. Johnny and

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:09.179
Clara, unaware of what the future holds for
them, face life happily,

00:02:09.179 --> 00:02:12.000
secure in their love.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:18.040
Hardworking Mrs. Borik, Peter's wife, lives
for her children alone. A kind, yielding woman,

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:22.060
she is resigned to a life of drudgery, and
ever-constant fear

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:27.890
that Clara and Agnes, and perhaps Johnny,
might fall victim to the disease that Peter

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:31.930
Borik carries.

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:38.020
It's time for lunch, and Johnny has been invited
to eat with the family. Peter cannot leave

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:42.510
his bed. He will not go to a sanatorium. He
does not believe

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.790
tuberculosis is catching.

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:50.280
He believes he can get well by staying in
bed. He wants to be near his neighbors so

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:54.890
they can drop in and see him. He likes Mrs.
Borik's cooking.

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:59.640
He wants to be home so he can call his wife
or his daughters at any time of the day or

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:04.600
night. The father's absence at meal time is
evident. But his

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:08.890
influence, both physical and spiritual, is
felt by the entire family every time they

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:10.390
eat.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:15.240
The door beyond the kitchen stove leads to
his room. From that room he can hear the familiar

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:20.930
voices of his family. At one time he was in
a sanatorium. He was

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:23.040
not a cooperative patient.

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:28.069
He felt there were too many restrictions.
That he did not feel sick. He left against

00:03:28.069 --> 00:03:32.610
medical advice. And since doctors cannot force
patients to remain in a

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:36.709
sanatorium, he could not be stopped.

00:03:36.709 --> 00:03:42.040
When he left the sanatorium, he left behind
the proper medical care, professional nursing

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:45.770
attention, and the rest routine which is so
essential to the

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:51.959
tuberculosis patient. Through his ignorance,
he left behind all hope, and brought home

00:03:51.959 --> 00:03:57.270
a disease which was to bring immeasurable
sorrow to his family.

00:03:57.270 --> 00:04:01.849
Peter's presence in the Boriks' household
has not changed the homemaking routine, although

00:04:01.849 --> 00:04:05.489
it should have, to ensure protection for the
family.

00:04:05.489 --> 00:04:10.680
Dishes used to serve his food are mixed with
those used by the rest of the family. His

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:15.300
bed linen goes in with the family laundry.
The handkerchiefs he uses

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:19.569
contain sputum, which is contaminated with
tuberculosis germs.

00:04:19.569 --> 00:04:25.190
The germs spread from person-to-person and
cause tuberculosis. Peter refuses to believe

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:30.540
this simple fact. Like measles, chicken pox
or scarlet fever,

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:33.320
tuberculosis is contagious.

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:39.320
Except for Peter Borik, the Borik family looks
healthy. They feel well. They don't think

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:43.550
they can catch Peter's disease. They don't
know a person may have

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:47.810
tuberculosis for three years and never have
any symptoms.

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:52.600
In recent weeks, Peter Borik's increasingly
bad condition has intensified his stubborn

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:57.830
streak. He talks to his family only in irritable
commands. His raucous

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.949
coughing has increased.

00:04:59.949 --> 00:05:05.650
The room behind the kitchen stove has become
a self-imposed cell, from which he bars time-tried

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:09.900
methods of tuberculosis cure. His failing
condition is

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:11.990
reflected in his lack of appetite.

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:17.150
Each day he leaves more and more food untouched
on the plate, which Mrs. Borik serves him

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:21.550
three times a day.

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:25.830
But tuberculosis workers know that Peter Borik
left the sanatorium against the advice of

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:29.410
physicians. They have been watching his case
ever since he acted

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:34.280
against the advice of specialists in the field
of tuberculosis cure and prevention.

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:39.810
Now they hope to convince him to return to
the sanatorium. Ever alert for cases such

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:44.630
as these, tuberculosis workers are certain
that Peter Borik will return

00:05:44.630 --> 00:05:47.540
in order to protect his wife and daughters.

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:54.540
Courteous and professional, the tuberculosis
worker visits the Borik household. This job

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:58.440
requires tact, for she does not want to frighten
Peter Borik back

00:05:58.440 --> 00:05:59.580
into the sanatorium.

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:04.800
She must convince him and Mrs. Borik that
he is spreading tuberculosis to his family

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:08.199
and friends. That he'll be able to receive
visitors frequently in the

00:06:08.199 --> 00:06:10.300
sanatorium.

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:15.350
But Mrs. Borik will have none of this. She
is too familiar with the wrath of her husband

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:22.350
and with his ideas of sanatoriums.

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:28.880
Mrs. Borik keeps the visit of the tuberculosis
worker a secret, both from Peter Borik and

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:30.699
from her children.

00:06:30.699 --> 00:06:35.850
That's why Johnny and Clara go ahead with
plans to get married. Each new day brings

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:40.070
to them new happiness as they plan for the
future.

00:06:40.070 --> 00:06:44.360
They are ignorant of the cloak of disease
that is enveloping the Borik household and

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:49.410
their lives. For how long can the human body
stand up under the strain

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:53.050
of bombardment of the tuberculosis germs?

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:58.080
These two youths, vigorous and gay, appear
to be happy and healthy as they await the

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:03.570
day of their marriage. But are they healthy?
The tuberculosis germ has

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:05.919
used them for targets.

00:07:05.919 --> 00:07:10.150
Back in the Borik household, they have been
exposed for months to the germs discharged

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:15.680
by Peter Borik. Is one or both to be a victim?
Perhaps they had come

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:22.680
in contact with tuberculosis by touching an
article contaminated by Peter Borik.

00:07:23.199 --> 00:07:29.490
In the spring, Johnny and Clara are married.
Peter Borik is too ill to attend the church

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:33.720
ceremony, but unknown to all, the mark of
his willfulness is with

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:34.500
them.

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:39.449
It is a threat to their happiness that could
have been avoided if Peter had gone to the

00:07:39.449 --> 00:07:44.580
sanatorium some time before. In fact, if Peter
had listened to sound

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:49.970
medical advice, or if his wife had acted upon
the suggestion of the tuberculosis worker,

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:54.500
he might have been cured by the time the wedding
took place.

00:07:54.500 --> 00:08:00.090
As Johnny takes Clara for his wife, and promisesto protect her in sickness and in health, little

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:03.400
does he realize that she had lived with open
tuberculous in

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:09.699
the household. Whether or not she has escaped
its attack remains to be seen.

00:08:09.699 --> 00:08:14.610
Their friends are equally ignorant of what
is going on in the Borik household. They can

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:19.030
see only the beautiful bride, and the dashing,
handsome groom. Two

00:08:19.030 --> 00:08:26.030
healthy, vigorous young people who are now
man and wife.

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:33.930
Back at the Borik household, usually somber
and quiet, the Boriks and their guests gather

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:38.699
for a wedding festivity. Everyone has visited
and paid his respects

00:08:38.699 --> 00:08:43.950
to Peter Borik in his sick room [background
comments].

00:08:43.950 --> 00:08:50.230
Preparations are made to have the bride cut
the wedding cake.

00:08:50.230 --> 00:08:54.700
Little does the happy couple suspect that
this ceremony is the backdrop for the tragedy

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:58.870
that is to follow.

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:03.130
But Johnny and Clara are unaware of the danger,
as they take over the operation of the Borik

00:09:03.130 --> 00:09:08.550
farm where they now live. His life with Clara
is a happy one.

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:13.010
One day, more than a year after their marriage,
Johnny comes home from the fields to find

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:17.820
that Clara is not feeling well. He questions
her and finds she is

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:24.820
suffering from headaches, becomes fatigued
easily and is running a slight fever.

00:09:25.770 --> 00:09:30.180
Clara then tells him she is going to have
a baby. And Johnny attributes the illness

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:37.180
to the coming child.

00:09:39.920 --> 00:09:45.820
But as time goes on, Johnny wonders, could
it be that in some mysterious manner, Peter's

00:09:45.820 --> 00:09:51.480
disease might be causing Clara's illness?

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:57.690
Clara's symptoms grow more evident daily.
She tires easily. The fresh farm foods cannot

00:09:57.690 --> 00:10:04.690
tempt her appetite.

00:10:06.860 --> 00:10:11.700
Johnny has made a decision. He is no longer
satisfied with Peter's advice that Clara eat

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:14.670
lots of food and stay out in the fresh air.

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:19.480
Johnny wants Clara to go to a competent doctor.
He fears for her life and that of their child.

00:10:19.480 --> 00:10:23.330
Clara has just had an x-ray of her lungs,
and a physical

00:10:23.330 --> 00:10:26.769
examination for tuberculosis at the sanatorium.

00:10:26.769 --> 00:10:32.160
The x-ray film seen in the viewer reveals
she has fallen victim to the disease. The

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:36.410
sanatorium doctor explains that everyone should
have a chest x-ray each

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:37.380
year.

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:43.820
He tells Mrs. Borik that tuberculosis is not
inherited and it is not caused by weak lungs.

00:10:43.820 --> 00:10:47.940
He points out that it's spread by germs from
one person to another

00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:53.890
and it runs 15 times higher in families where
there is a history of tuberculosis.

00:10:53.890 --> 00:11:00.890
The doctor ponders. He wonders where Clara
could have contracted tuberculosis.

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:06.550
He tells Mrs. Borik that one does not have
to look sick to be sick with tuberculosis.

00:11:06.550 --> 00:11:10.519
The doctor also points out that the earlier
tuberculosis is detected,

00:11:10.519 --> 00:11:13.230
the easier the disease is to cure.

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:19.930
The body must build up a resistance to the
germ. Clara has far advanced tuberculosis.

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:22.420
If she'd only come to a doctor earlier...

00:11:22.420 --> 00:11:27.740
If she'd only been checked periodically for
tuberculosis...How, he asked Mrs. Borik, could

00:11:27.740 --> 00:11:29.899
Clara have caught tuberculosis?

00:11:29.899 --> 00:11:36.899
Mrs. Borik knows now. Sadly she recites the
story of Peter for the first time. Peter,

00:11:37.110 --> 00:11:41.800
her husband, was in a sanatorium for treatment.

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:47.180
But Peter didn't like the sanatorium. He didn't
feel sick. He didn't realize that he should

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:50.430
be willing to remain hospitalized so that
his family would be

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:53.120
protected against the disease.

00:11:53.120 --> 00:12:00.120
He didn't believe what the doctors told him.
One night, Peter left the sanatorium. Peter

00:12:00.300 --> 00:12:05.660
Borik left the sanatorium against medical
advice.

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:10.450
The full impact of Peter's willfulness; his
persistent rejection of the truth, has come

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:14.660
home. Johnny wants Clara to go to the sanatorium.

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:20.240
He feels that both her life and the life of
their child might be saved. He knows if she'd

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:24.890
gone earlier, she would not have to stay so
long in the sanatorium.

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:27.730
But Peter has taught his lesson well.

00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:33.860
Clara too rejects sanatorium care. She will
take her chances of getting well at home.

00:12:33.860 --> 00:12:36.890
Her father had told her that once you enter
the sanatorium, you would

00:12:36.890 --> 00:12:38.470
surely die.

00:12:38.470 --> 00:12:45.470
Poor Clara. She believes this wrong advice.
What better attention could she get in a sanatorium?

00:12:46.519 --> 00:12:49.970
she asks herself and her husband.

00:12:49.970 --> 00:12:55.930
But she has no way of telling if she is getting
better or worse. At the sanatorium she would

00:12:55.930 --> 00:12:57.529
be x-rayed regularly.

00:12:57.529 --> 00:13:04.529
Sputum tests would be taken. Surgery would
be recommended if necessary. The progress

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:11.950
of her disease would be noted regularly.

00:13:13.839 --> 00:13:19.760
Johnny begs Clara again to go to a sanatorium.
Complicated by the fact that she is expecting

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:24.680
a baby, tuberculosis works quickly in Clara.
She loses ground

00:13:24.680 --> 00:13:31.680
rapidly.

00:13:32.829 --> 00:13:38.140
Tuberculosis takes its toll. And with Clara's
death, another life is taken. The life of

00:13:38.140 --> 00:13:44.490
her unborn child.

00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:50.350
Clara has paid with her life. Johnny is not
very expressive, but he misses Clara terribly.

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:55.600
They had had so little time together. None
of their plans, the

00:13:55.600 --> 00:14:02.600
plans of youth, had come to fruition.

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:15.410
He remembers her vivacity. Her winsome smile.
Her dark curls. And her tender touch.

00:14:18.389 --> 00:14:25.389
He realizes that all this is lost to him forever
because of a disease which need not have happened

00:14:26.870 --> 00:14:33.870
if it had not been for one man's willfulness.

00:14:42.079 --> 00:14:46.740
And in remembering Clara and her youth, he
thinks of Agnes, who has gone to work in a

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:51.200
factory. Will the pattern of tragedy be repeated
in lively Agnes, who

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:54.170
has such a desire to live?

00:14:54.170 --> 00:14:59.139
Johnny has talked to the tuberculosis worker.
She has urged Johnny to prevail upon Agnes

00:14:59.139 --> 00:15:00.790
to have a chest x-ray.

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:05.470
She pointed out to Johnny that tuberculosis
takes its greatest toll among young people

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:11.940
from 15 to 35 years of age. Johnny tells Agnes
this. He asks her to

00:15:11.940 --> 00:15:14.139
have an x-ray.

00:15:14.139 --> 00:15:18.010
After all, he reasons, if you find out that
you haven't caught tuberculosis from your

00:15:18.010 --> 00:15:21.740
father or Clara, you have nothing to worry
about.

00:15:21.740 --> 00:15:26.550
If you do find out you have tuberculosis,
you can go to the sanatorium before your case

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:31.500
becomes hopeless. He tells her that many people
have the tuberculosis

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:33.540
germ in their bodies.

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:39.269
As long as the resistance is kept up, the
germ remains inactive. He tells Agnes she

00:15:39.269 --> 00:15:42.550
has been working hard at her factory job,
that the germ may have gotten a

00:15:42.550 --> 00:15:44.449
foothold in her body.

00:15:44.449 --> 00:15:50.480
He reasons with her. But Agnes can't be reasoned
with. She has a streak of her father's willfulness

00:15:50.480 --> 00:15:53.480
in her. It is fate, she decides.

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:58.829
If my father was sick with tuberculosis, and
my sister died from it, I will too. It's just

00:15:58.829 --> 00:16:02.910
a matter of time and I might as well enjoy
life.

00:16:02.910 --> 00:16:09.910
Secretly, Agnes feels that she too might have
the disease.

00:16:14.810 --> 00:16:20.329
Many thousands of tuberculous sick are among
us. Everything they touch, cough, or spit

00:16:20.329 --> 00:16:27.329
on is infected with the tuberculosis germ.

00:16:28.940 --> 00:16:33.600
They're a constant source of danger to the
people who come in contact with them. But

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:37.139
they go blithely on their way, either unaware
that they have the

00:16:37.139 --> 00:16:44.139
disease, or unwilling to do anything about
it.

00:16:46.190 --> 00:16:53.190
Agnes is afraid. She does not want to know
the truth.

00:16:57.740 --> 00:17:04.260
But the truth cannot be denied and shut out
forever. It must come out. And Agnes, despite

00:17:04.260 --> 00:17:11.260
her stubbornness, cannot refuse to acknowledge
that she is sick.

00:17:14.269 --> 00:17:21.269
Too sick to work efficiently.

00:17:32.059 --> 00:17:37.749
Many industries have case-finding programs.
Industry wants to protect its workers against

00:17:37.749 --> 00:17:43.739
tuberculosis.

00:17:43.739 --> 00:17:50.739
An x-ray is painless and takes only a moment.

00:17:53.909 --> 00:17:58.629
X-ray is used to find tuberculosis among apparently
healthy people as well as among persons who

00:17:58.629 --> 00:18:04.909
have had contact with a tuberculosis patient.

00:18:04.909 --> 00:18:10.729
They find her disease in the factory x-ray.
And, as is true in industry, when tuberculosis

00:18:10.729 --> 00:18:17.729
is found, she is required to leave her work.

00:18:19.669 --> 00:18:26.470
Agnes has tuberculosis. No longer does Mrs.
Borik need to be convinced. Tuberculosis killed

00:18:26.470 --> 00:18:30.899
one daughter, and she is determined to save
Agnes.

00:18:30.899 --> 00:18:36.149
Mrs. Borik will defy Peter at any cost. Knowing
that his ignorance has caused this tragedy,

00:18:36.149 --> 00:18:40.440
she is going to have a chest x-ray herself.
Johnny will have one

00:18:40.440 --> 00:18:42.809
too.

00:18:42.809 --> 00:18:47.529
Agnes has finally reconciled to going to the
sanatorium. She sees that her father is not

00:18:47.529 --> 00:18:51.799
getting any better at home, and that Clara
came home only to die.

00:18:51.799 --> 00:18:56.889
She realizes that if she gives up six months
of time now to sanatorium treatment, she may

00:18:56.889 --> 00:19:00.809
well save her life.

00:19:00.809 --> 00:19:07.809
Happily, Agnes' disease has been caught early.
She will be able to recover from tuberculosis,

00:19:17.629 --> 00:19:20.119
and lead a happy, normal life.

00:19:20.119 --> 00:19:27.119
She now realizes tuberculosis can be cured.
It is not a death sentence.

00:19:28.729 --> 00:19:34.129
Mrs. Borik knows, and Johnny knows, that by
going to the sanatorium early, Agnes' chances

00:19:34.129 --> 00:19:40.269
for recovery are enhanced.

00:19:40.269 --> 00:19:43.789
Johnny and Mrs. Borik return to their house
of sorrow, determined that there shall be

00:19:43.789 --> 00:19:48.389
no more needless suffering and death. They
have been examined, and they

00:19:48.389 --> 00:19:50.710
happily are not victims of Peter's disease.

00:19:50.710 --> 00:19:57.710
It will not be a simple matter to return Peter
to a sanatorium, but their minds are made

00:19:58.409 --> 00:20:03.320
up. They know he is wrong in staying home.
He must go back to the

00:20:03.320 --> 00:20:06.119
tuberculosis hospital.

00:20:06.119 --> 00:20:11.210
Last year, more than 50,000 American men,
women and children died in our country, because

00:20:11.210 --> 00:20:14.580
they made the wrong decisions when they still
could have been

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:14.929
saved.

00:20:14.929 --> 00:20:20.309
Don't let the tragedy of the Borik family
repeat in your home! Remember, no home is

00:20:20.309 --> 00:20:25.090
safe until all homes are safe.

00:20:25.090 --> 00:20:27.450
[Music]

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:34.450
[The End, A Capital Film Production.]

